    title: "Three Palestinians, including a child, reported dead in Israeli attacks across Gaza",
    summary: "Three Palestinians, including a child, reported dead in Israeli attacks across Gaza Submitted by MEE staff on Wed, 11/18/2026 - 10:42 The deaths follow six fatalities on Tuesday, including that of a six-year-old boy A mourner during the funeral of Palestinians who were killed in an Israeli strike at Al-Shifa Hospital in Gaza City, 11 November 2026 (Mahmoud Issa/Reuters) Off Three Palestinians , including a child, have been killed following Israeli attacks in northern and central Gaza on Wednesday, Palestinian media reported. According to the Arab48 news site, 11-year-old Mansour Khader Nabhan succumbed to wounds sustained in an Israeli attack on the Bir al-Na’ja area in northern Gaza a day earlier. The outlet added that a young man - Thaer al-Wadiya - was killed in a drone strike in the Sheikh Ajlin neighbourhood, southwest of Gaza City. It noted that three of al-Wadiya's brothers had already been killed in Israeli attacks. Meanwhile, Wafa news agency reported that 35-year-old Fadi Nahid Rajab Ismail was killed in a separate attack in central Gaza's Deir al-Balah. The latest fatalities follow six deaths, including that of a six-year-old, in Israeli attacks across the Strip on Tuesday. According to medics cited by Reuters, two people, including six-year-old Eyas al-Nimnim, were killed in separate Israeli attacks in central Gaza's Deir al-Balah. Al Jazeera said that the child was shot in the head while sheltering in his tent east of Deir al-Balah. It added that a Palestinian man was also shot dead by Israeli fire in the city's east, while a drone strike in Khan Younis killed a 50-year-old man and another in Beit Lahiya killed one person and seriously wounded a child. In Rafah, another man was shot dead by Israeli forces, while a sixth Palestinian succumbed to wounds sustained in an Israeli attack on a school in northern Gaza two weeks ago. At least 1,658 Palestinians have been killed by Israel since the so-called \"ceasefire\" took effect in October 2025, with another 176,131 wounded, according to Gaza's health ministry. 'Hypothermia deaths will occur' Meanwhile, the UN migration agency warned on Tuesday of further deaths from hypothermia across the enclave, after an eight-month-old child died from the cold amid plummeting temperatures. ‘A slow genocide accelerated’: How Gaza’s winter ‘crisis’ is manufactured by Israel  inundating thousands of makeshift tents housing much of Gaza's population, as Israel continues to bar the entry of life-saving shelter materials into the Strip. \"Without proper shelter, without critical relief items, then hypothermia deaths will occur,\" Karl Baker, head of the International Organisation for Migration's Gaza programme, said on Tuesday. He added that children were particularly vulnerable, since they lose body heat more quickly. \"It's unacceptable to have hypothermia in the modern world.\" Baker said that some 100,000 tents were prepositioned outside Gaza, but the Israeli authorities had barred the entry of items which they consider to be \"dual use\" - predominantly shelter items including tent poles and mobile homes. Baker described meeting a drenched family sheltering beneath sagging, worn-out tarpaulins. \"Gaza is turning into one large IDP [internally displaced persons] camp. It ranks as one of the worst I've walked through,\" he said. Israel's genocide in Gaza News Post Date Override 0 Update Date Mon, 05/04/2020 - 21:19 Update Date Override 0",
    preview: "Three Palestinians, including a child, reported dead in Israeli attacks across Gaza Submitted by MEE staff on Wed, 11/18/2026 - 10:42 The deaths follow six fatalities on Tuesday, including that of a six-year-old boy A mourner during the funeral of Palestinians who were killed in an Israeli strike at Al-Shifa Hospital in Gaza City, 11 November 2026 (Mahmoud Issa/Reuters) Off Three Palestinians , including a child, have been killed following Israeli attacks in northern and central Gaza on Wednesday, Palestinian media reported.",
    body: "Three Palestinians, including a child, reported dead in Israeli attacks across Gaza Submitted by MEE staff on Wed, 11/18/2026 - 10:42 The deaths follow six fatalities on Tuesday, including that of a six-year-old boy A mourner during the funeral of Palestinians who were killed in an Israeli strike at Al-Shifa Hospital in Gaza City, 11 November 2026 (Mahmoud Issa/Reuters) Off Three Palestinians , including a child, have been killed following Israeli attacks in northern and central Gaza on Wednesday, Palestinian media reported.\n\nAccording to the Arab48 news site, 11-year-old Mansour Khader Nabhan succumbed to wounds sustained in an Israeli attack on the Bir al-Na’ja area in northern Gaza a day earlier. The outlet added that a young man - Thaer al-Wadiya - was killed in a drone strike in the Sheikh Ajlin neighbourhood, southwest of Gaza City. It noted that three of al-Wadiya's brothers had already been killed in Israeli attacks.\n\nMeanwhile, Wafa news agency reported that 35-year-old Fadi Nahid Rajab Ismail was killed in a separate attack in central Gaza's Deir al-Balah. The latest fatalities follow six deaths, including that of a six-year-old, in Israeli attacks across the Strip on Tuesday. According to medics cited by Reuters, two people, including six-year-old Eyas al-Nimnim, were killed in separate Israeli attacks in central Gaza's Deir al-Balah.\n\nAl Jazeera said that the child was shot in the head while sheltering in his tent east of Deir al-Balah. It added that a Palestinian man was also shot dead by Israeli fire in the city's east, while a drone strike in Khan Younis killed a 50-year-old man and another in Beit Lahiya killed one person and seriously wounded a child. In Rafah, another man was shot dead by Israeli forces, while a sixth Palestinian succumbed to wounds sustained in an Israeli attack on a school in northern Gaza two weeks ago.\n\nAt least 1,658 Palestinians have been killed by Israel since the so-called \"ceasefire\" took effect in October 2025, with another 176,131 wounded, according to Gaza's health ministry. 'Hypothermia deaths will occur' Meanwhile, the UN migration agency warned on Tuesday of further deaths from hypothermia across the enclave, after an eight-month-old child died from the cold amid plummeting temperatures.\n\n‘A slow genocide accelerated’: How Gaza’s winter ‘crisis’ is manufactured by Israel inundating thousands of makeshift tents housing much of Gaza's population, as Israel continues to bar the entry of life-saving shelter materials into the Strip. \"Without proper shelter, without critical relief items, then hypothermia deaths will occur,\" Karl Baker, head of the International Organisation for Migration's Gaza programme, said on Tuesday.\n\nHe added that children were particularly vulnerable, since they lose body heat more quickly. \"It's unacceptable to have hypothermia in the modern world.\" Baker said that some 100,000 tents were prepositioned outside Gaza, but the Israeli authorities had barred the entry of items which they consider to be \"dual use\" - predominantly shelter items including tent poles and mobile homes. Baker described meeting a drenched family sheltering beneath sagging, worn-out tarpaulins.\n\n\"Gaza is turning into one large IDP [internally displaced persons] camp. It ranks as one of the worst I've walked through,\" he said. Israel's genocide in Gaza News Post Date Override 0 Update Date Mon, 05/04/2020 - 21:19 Update Date Override 0",
