    title: "Trump's Board of Peace says Gaza ceasefire has delivered 'nothing visible'",
    summary: "Trump's Board of Peace says Gaza ceasefire has delivered 'nothing visible' US President Donald Trump's Board of Peace, the body supposedly tasked with overseeing the end to fighting in Gaza, has accused both Israel and Hamas of failing to end hostilities, leaving the Palestinian enclave's population in dire need. The 12-page Board of Peace report, seen by Reuters, is the body's second to the United Nations Security Council since the US-backed ceasefire came into effect 13 months ago. It offers a \"sobering assessment of progress made since then\", Reuters said. The board, established and headed by Trump, is expected to present the report's findings to a meeting of the council in New York at the end of November. “The distance between what has been agreed and what is happening on the ground nonetheless remains the principal risk to the process,” the report said, warning that “a ceasefire that delivers nothing visible cannot be sustained indefinitely.” Since the ceasefire, Israeli attacks have killed more than 1,431 people, including at least 300 children, and wounded 5,026. The office of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and a spokesperson for the political office of Hamas did not immediately respond to requests for comment on the report. “There is no ceasefire in Gaza. People talk about a ceasefire but at best it’s a reduced fire,” Chris Sidoti, a member of the UN Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory , told MEE's Expert Witness podcast this week.",
    preview: "Trump's Board of Peace says Gaza ceasefire has delivered 'nothing visible' US President Donald Trump's Board of Peace, the body supposedly tasked with overseeing the end to fighting in Gaza, has accused both Israel and Hamas of failing to end hostilities, leaving the Palestinian enclave's population in dire need. The 12-page Board of Peace report, seen by Reuters, is the body's second to the United Nations Security Council since the US-backed ceasefire came into effect 13 months ago.",
    body: "Trump's Board of Peace says Gaza ceasefire has delivered 'nothing visible' US President Donald Trump's Board of Peace, the body supposedly tasked with overseeing the end to fighting in Gaza, has accused both Israel and Hamas of failing to end hostilities, leaving the Palestinian enclave's population in dire need. The 12-page Board of Peace report, seen by Reuters, is the body's second to the United Nations Security Council since the US-backed ceasefire came into effect 13 months ago.\n\nIt offers a \"sobering assessment of progress made since then\", Reuters said. The board, established and headed by Trump, is expected to present the report's findings to a meeting of the council in New York at the end of November. “The distance between what has been agreed and what is happening on the ground nonetheless remains the principal risk to the process,” the report said, warning that “a ceasefire that delivers nothing visible cannot be sustained indefinitely.” Since the ceasefire, Israeli attacks have killed more than 1,431 people, including at least 300 children, and wounded 5,026.\n\nThe office of Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu and a spokesperson for the political office of Hamas did not immediately respond to requests for comment on the report. “There is no ceasefire in Gaza. People talk about a ceasefire but at best it’s a reduced fire,” Chris Sidoti, a member of the UN Commission of Inquiry on the Occupied Palestinian Territory , told MEE's Expert Witness podcast this week.",
